SUMMARY: 6 confirmed bugs in HikariCP core, spanning array bounds violations, null pointer crashes, incorrect field assignments, reversed type checks, state tracking errors, and missing input validation. All have verified fixes.

POINTS:
- [src/main/java/com/zaxxer/hikari/util/ConcurrentBag.java:402] getStateCounts() throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException when entries are in STATE_REMOVED or STATE_RESERVED, as negative state values are used directly as array indices — fix: ++states[e.getState() + 2];
- [src/main/java/com/zaxxer/hikari/HikariConfig.java:893] setCredentialsProviderClassName() writes to exceptionOverrideClassName instead of credentialsProviderClassName, causing the getter to always return null — fix: this.credentialsProviderClassName = credentialsProviderClassName;
- [src/main/java/com/zaxxer/hikari/pool/ProxyStatement.java:230] getGeneratedKeys() throws NullPointerException when delegate returns null, lacking the null check present in getResultSet() — fix: add null check before calling ProxyFactory.getProxyResultSet()
- [src/main/java/com/zaxxer/hikari/pool/HikariConnectionProvider.java:128] isUnwrappableAs() and unwrap() reverse isAssignableFrom() operands, causing valid unwrap types to incorrectly fail — fix: unwrapType.isAssignableFrom(HikariConnectionProvider.class)
- [src/main/java/com/zaxxer/hikari/pool/ProxyConnection.java:395] rollback(Savepoint) incorrectly sets isCommitStateDirty = true, causing an unnecessary rollback on close() — fix: isCommitStateDirty = false;
- [src/main/java/com/zaxxer/hikari/HikariConfig.java:757] setKeepaliveTime() accepts negative values without validation, silently discarding them later — fix: throw IllegalArgumentException for negative inputs

